{"born":[{"text":"b132719eae","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":16,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b132719eae","mother":5,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":12,"rewritten":false},{"text":"5a5de32ef5","mother":4,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code improves safety by strictly avoiding definitively poisonous fruits unless starvation is imminent, using 'felt' hunger to prevent overeating when partially full, and prioritizing tasting for mixed/uncertain histories to detect toxicity shifts while managing risk.","ms":8339},{"text":"b132719eae","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":21,"rewritten":false},{"text":"355cd603ce","mother":11,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":10,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b132719eae","mother":20,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b132719eae","mother":20,"rewritten":false},{"text":"d9951d6588","mother":21,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes safety by requiring three positive samples before confidently eating, avoids known poisonous fruits entirely, and uses 'taste' to resolve uncertainty for novel or ambiguous fruits only when hunger is moderate, preventing starvation while minimizing risk.","ms":6748},{"text":"5bdb418117","mother":16,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes safety by rejecting fruits with unconfirmed harms and zero feeds, while aggressively collecting proven safe fruits (2+ feeds) and only tasting novel ones when hunger is low enough to spare the risk of a bad bite.","ms":8521},{"text":"19cbe103ee","mother":13,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes avoiding known poisonous fruits (those with more harms than feeds) and immediately eats proven safe ones. For unknown fruits, it chooses 'taste' to gather data safely, only resorting to risky behavior when starvation is imminent, ensuring long-term survival through learning rather than blind risk-taking.","ms":10578},{"text":"b132719eae","mother"